  "narrative": {
    "intro": "RTX reported $3.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. RTX received 680 awards so far, with an average award size of $5.5M and obligations down 48.2% year over year. The Department of Defense accounted for $3.8B of obligations in FY2026 to date. RTX’s FY21 obligations were $3.7B, FY22 obligations were $8B, FY23 obligations were $8.2B, FY24 obligations were $5B, and FY25 obligations were $7.3B. Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing is RTX’s largest market with $1.6B in obligations, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing with $806M and Aircraft Manufacturing with $805M. Other meaningful markets include Other Support Activities for Air Transportation with $515M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) with $36.6M. Smaller reported markets include Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $8.7M and Bolt, Nut, Screw, Rivet, and Washer Manufacturing at $8.4M.",
    "sections": [
