        "heading": "How does RTX's FY2026 federal business compare with prior years?",
        "body": "RTX obligated $3.8B in FY2026 to date. RTX’s obligations were $3.7B in FY21, $8B in FY22, $8.2B in FY23, $5B in FY24, and $7.3B in FY25. RTX’s obligations are down 48.2% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are RTX's biggest federal customers and what markets do they buy?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $3.8B from RTX in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $659K and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $1.7K. Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing is the largest market at $1.6B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $806M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $805M."
      }
